  "query_preview": "../Friday through Monday/...No major changes to be \nseen in the extended forecast with a ridge of high pressure \nbuilding in over the gulf come Friday. This will finally dislodge \nthe weak troughing over the panhandle and usher in more consistent\ndry conditions this weekend and overall benign weather. As \nmentioned in previous discussions, a tightening gradient early \nFriday favoring north south oriented channels is expected to bring\nabout some stout northerly winds. However these should quickly \ndiminish through the afternoon hours Friday with winds across the \ninner channels and coastal waters largely falling to 10 kt or \nless. With the drier conditions, localized sea breezes are \nexpected through the weekend but should not be particularly \nimpactful. \n\nThe main question in the long term remains whether a low develops\nin the northern gulf to take a swipe at the northern panhandle \nearly next week. Models are still not sold on the idea, though \nthere is a slight trend for a majority of the associated \nprecipitation to remain over the interior. Overall though the main\ntakeaway is still for another round of more summer-like weather \nthis weekend with fairly dry conditions and daytime highs to \nrebound to the mid 60s to around 70 for most of the panhandle.",
